From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:19:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: draw effect graphs the way Windows does, with the
 built-in effects Office uses

On Windows each effect builds a transform graph whose transforms house the
shaders run for every output pixel, and the built-in effects are made with the
same framework applications get for their own (the Effects overview says so in
as many words).  Wine had the graph objects but nothing that drew them:
DrawImage of an effect's output only printed "Unhandled image", and the built-in
effects were empty shells.  PowerPoint draws Shadow and 2D affine transform
effects directly, and its Windows.UI.Composition cross fade is an
ArithmeticComposite graph.

effect_render.c works a graph back from what is to be drawn, using only the
transforms' own interfaces: MapOutputRectToInputRects says what each input must
supply, the inputs (bitmaps, command lists, other effects) are drawn into
intermediate textures, and each draw transform's pixel shader runs with the
inputs D2D hands custom shaders (SCENE_POSITION, TEXCOORDn with the size of a
pixel in zw).  Offset, bounds adjustment, border and blend transforms are drawn
too.  Only what the clip or target shows is rendered, and the result is
composited with DrawImage's composite mode.  The inputs of a pass are bound
after its output, since a view still bound for output reads as nothing.

ID2D1DrawInfo keeps input descriptions, output buffers and pixel shader
constants; SetOutputBuffer validates as on Windows.  PrepareForRender is called
before the first draw and after properties, the graph or the DPI changed, with
SetDrawInfo coming before it.

Flood, ArithmeticComposite, Composite, Crop, 2D affine transform, Gaussian
blur, Shadow and Grayscale are now real effects with their own transforms and
shaders, and GetImageLocalBounds reports the bounds of effects.

The Windows-derived expectations for affine bounds and figures, crop bounds,
flood bounds and surface, grayscale colours, a custom pixel shader and
SetOutputBuffer now hold and lose their todo_wine.  test_effect_rendering checks
the formulas the documentation gives for arithmetic composite, composite modes,
nested effects, image rectangles, shadow colour, blur and command list inputs;
it was not run on Windows.  d2d1: 17641 tests, 0 failures, on the GL and the
Vulkan renderer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4b42eb3c07872d82fa9c981694dba01ae65df938)

